<title>UK: SOCCER-SCOTLAND 2 AUSTRIA 0 WORLD CUP QUALIFIER - RESULT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SCOTLAND 2 AUSTRIA 0 WORLD CUP QUALIFIER - RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>GLASGOW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scotland beat Austria 2-0</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in their World Cup European group four qualifier</p>
<p>on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Kevin Gallacher 24, 77</p>
<p>Attendance: 43,295</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Scotland - 1-Jim Leighton; 2-Craig Burley, 4-Colin</p>
<p>Calderwood, 5-Colin Hendry, 3-Tom Boyd, 6-Tosh McKinlay, 7-Kevin</p>
<p>Gallacher (16-Ally McCoist 84), 10-Gary McAllister (15-Paul</p>
<p>McStay 88), 8-Paul Lambert, 9-Darren Jackson (17-Billy McGinlay</p>
<p>75), 11-John Collins.</p>
<p>Austria - 1-Michael Konsel; 5-Wolfgang Feiersinger, 7-Franz</p>
<p>Aigner (13-Andreas Ogris 81), 4-Anton Pfeffer, 3-Peter Schottel</p>
<p>(15-Walter Kogler 46), 2-Markus Schopp, 6-Andreas Heraf,</p>
<p>10-Andreas Herzog, 8-Arnold Wetl, 11-Peter Stoger (14-Ivica</p>
<p>Bastic 67), 9-Anton Polster</p>
<p>Referee: Nikolai Levnikov (Russia)</p>
<p>   Standings	 Pl  W   D   L   F   A  Pts</p>
<p> Scotland	    6   4   2   0   7   0   14</p>
<p> Austria	     4   2   1   1   3   3    7</p>
<p> Sweden		4   2   0   2   7   4    6</p>
<p> Estonia	     4   1   1   2   1   3    4</p>
<p> Belarus	     4   1   1   2   3   7    4</p>
<p> Latvia		4   0   1   3   3   7    1</p>
<p>Next matches: April 30 Austria v Estonia, Sweden v Scotland,</p>
<p>Latvia v Belarus</p>
</text>
